  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SHAPE 2 - Social Housing Advancement and Poverty Eradication</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">More than 60% of Kenya&apos;s urban population lives in slums, which are expected to double in size in 15 years. Slum dwellers generally do not have title to the land they occupy, and have limited access to clean water or useable toilets, or credit facilities. Without a collective voice, people living in the slums do not possess the ability to engage with the relevant authorities to change this situation. This project seeks to address some of these problems and will benefit tens of thousands of slum dwellers in 18 slums across Kenya.  It will promote community savings and make affordable loans more widely available &#x2013; for both housing and small businesses. People living in the slums will learn about low-cost building technologies and improved water and sanitation facilities.  Formation of community groups will enable them to participate in urban planning and achieve better services for their communities. As a result, people will have better housing, sanitation and improved economic prospects and local government will be more responsive to the collective voice of slum dwellers.</narrative>
  </description>
